column2:
Salutation to Kala, the god, to the three gods, to the three forms, to him of unmanifest and manifest form, who goes endlessly without end;
skandapuran:44:36	to him whose form is Rik, Yajus and Saman, all-knowing, salutation to you; source of existence, lord of the world, beloved of Uma, salutation to you.
skandapuran:44:37	Salutation to you, god, slayer of asuras, slayer of Tripura; Sadyojata, Aghora — salutation to you, lord of Purusha.
skandapuran:44:38	Victory! Salutation again and again to Kalagnirudra, to Samvarta; salutation to you, Hrishikeshvara Rudra, lord of Purusha.
skandapuran:44:39	Salutation to Shambhava, to Mayobhava; salutation to you, Shankara; giver of boons to Brahma, Vishnu and Indra, salutation to you, three-eyed one.
skandapuran:44:40	Salutation to Shrikantha, Nilakantha, bearer of the half-moon; salutation to you who wear a garland of skulls and bear the khatvanga;
skandapuran:44:41	salutation to you with the trident in hand, adorned with serpent ornaments; salutation to you, bearer of the Pinaka; salutation to you, great lord.
skandapuran:44:42	To Sharva, to him of all forms, moving and unmoving, salutation to you. By the fickleness of my tongue you have been wearied by me, lord;
skandapuran:44:43	forgive me, lord of gods, here and hereafter; there is no other equal to you, lord of gods, husband of Uma.
